      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the sum of the roots of the given quadratic equation, we will first simplify it into the standard form \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\).\n\nGiven: \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\)\n\nExpanding the equation:\n\\[(x - 5)^2 = x^2 - 10x + 25\\]\n\nSetting it equal to zero to find the roots:\n\\[x^2 - 10x + 25 = 0\\]\n\nNow, to find the sum of the roots, we use the property of a quadratic equation described by \\(a*x^2 + b*x + c = 0\\). Its sum of roots is given by \\(-b/a\\).\n\nIn our equation, \\(a = 1\\). Therefore, the sum of roots is:\n\\[-(-10)/1 = 10\\]\n\nHence, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
